  The submit handler becomes [38;5;153mconst { valid, errors, values } = validateForm(form, LOGIN_RULES)[39m and, on failure,
  [38;5;153mconsole.error("Validation errors:", errors)[39m — same console-only reporting as today, since display stays each form's
  business.

  [1mTwo behavior changes worth naming.[0m Per-field messages replace the single "Missing required fields" string. And because
  [38;5;153mvaluesFromForm[39m trims, a whitespace-only username now fails where it previously passed. Both are improvements, but
  they are changes. The [38;5;153mminLength(8)[39m on password is a suggestion — say the word and I'll drop it so the migration is
  behavior-identical apart from the trim.

  [1mError handling:[0m malformed rules (a non-function in a rule array, [38;5;153mvalidateForm[39m called on a non-form element) throw
  [38;5;153mTypeError[39m immediately. Those are programming errors, and failing loudly beats silently skipping a check that someone
  thinks is running.

  [1mThe tooling fork.[0m The repo has no test runner, and there's a real constraint: [38;5;153mpackage.json[39m has no [38;5;153m"type"[39m field, so
  Node treats [38;5;153m.js[39m as CommonJS — which is what [38;5;153msrc/index.js[39m and [38;5;153msrc/utils.js[39m rely on. A browser loading [38;5;153mvalidation.js[39m as
  a module doesn't care, but a Node test importing it does. Three ways out:

  - [1mAdd [38;5;153m"type": "module"[39m and convert [38;5;153msrc/[0m — the two [38;5;153msrc[39m files are three lines each; converting [38;5;153mrequire[39m/[38;5;153mmodule.exports[39m to
    [38;5;153mimport[39m/[38;5;153mexport[39m makes the whole package consistently ESM. Costs: touches two files unrelated to your request.
  - [1mName it [38;5;153mvalidation.mjs[0m — root config untouched, Node tests work immediately. Costs: some static servers don't map
    [38;5;153m.mjs[39m to a JS MIME type, and the browser then refuses the module. A real, annoying failure mode.
  - [1mNo unit tests[0m — verify by hand in the browser. Costs: the shared module everything will depend on has no tests.

  [1mMy recommendation: the first[0m, with [38;5;153mnode --test[39m (built into Node, zero dependencies) and a [38;5;153mtest/validation.test.js[39m
  covering the rule factories, per-field error collection, and trimming. It's the option where nothing is booby-trapped
  later, and the "unrelated" churn is six lines.

